    "contentUrl": "https://content.jwplatform.com/videos/NjSOnQ8V-K3AjnAEN.mp4",
    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make Bohemian orange chicken, an easy and delicious dish inspired by duck a l'orange and bohemian-style roast duck. He generously salts chicken thighs on both sides and sears them in a heavy-duty pan with olive oil until they turn golden brown. He then makes an onion caramel by cooking diced onions, sugar, and salt, which is used to create a sauce that pairs perfectly with the orange flavor. The chicken is added to the sauce, which is made with orange and lemon juice, chicken broth, cinnamon, cayenne pepper, and black pepper. The dish is finished when the liquids come to a boil, and the chicken is cooked through and ready to serve for dinner!",
